Z||000000||Fiasco||04-11-2000||04:27 AM||||I am thinking about painting my '85 SE and am wondering if it is worth taking the panels off and having them sprayed, or do I leave them on the car and do the door jambs/overspray areas myself? (The car is red now and I'm probably going to go with black)||||reg||5
Z||000001||mutfish||04-11-2000||07:56 AM||||I changed my '88 GT from white to black,and imo the only way to properly cover all the edges is to dissasemble everything...I did it that way and still missed a few minute spots....||||reg||1
Z||000002||Monkeyman||04-11-2000||09:42 AM||||All depends how picky you are and how much $$ you have to spend.  Unless you plan on painting the entire car yourself, you might not be happy with a professional job on everything but the jambs, etc.  It might have a different look.  I would suggest, assuming you have the cash, letting a qualified body shop do the entire thing.  It might cost more now, but might be less problems in the future.||||reg||1
